WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.110
In this video, you open the console of a running virtual machine and log in. The console works even before the guest has a network connection.

00:00:08.110 --> 00:00:15.370
The virtual machine demo-console is running. You open its console from the Virtual Machines list.

00:00:15.370 --> 00:00:18.460
Select Console in its row.

00:00:18.460 --> 00:00:23.810
Open in WebVNC shows the graphical screen of the virtual machine.

00:00:23.810 --> 00:00:28.970
Open in Serial Console shows its serial text terminal instead.

00:00:28.970 --> 00:00:36.720
Select Open in WebVNC. The console opens in its own browser window.

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:42.590
The console connects and shows the login prompt of openSUSE Leap.

00:00:42.590 --> 00:00:45.140
Type the user name, sles,

00:00:45.140 --> 00:00:51.240
and the password that cloud-init set when the virtual machine first started.

00:00:51.240 --> 00:00:58.420
You are logged in. Run a command, for example, to list the network addresses.

00:00:58.420 --> 00:01:06.550
The toolbar at the top sends special keys, such as Control Alt Delete, to the virtual machine.

00:01:06.550 --> 00:01:13.671
You can now reach any running virtual machine from its console. Next, you stop, start, and restart a virtual machine.
